) VALUES (
    'history-of-freestyle-skiing',
    '{"en": "History of Freestyle Skiing: From Rebels to Champions", "de": "Geschichte des Freestyle-Skiing: Von Rebellen zu Champions", "fr": "Histoire du ski freestyle : Des rebelles aux champions", "it": "Storia dello sci freestyle: Da ribelli a campioni", "es": "Historia del esquí estilo libre: De rebeldes a campeones", "pt": "História do esqui estilo livre: De rebeldes a campeões", "nl": "Geschiedenis van freestyle skiën: Van rebellen tot kampioenen", "ar": "تاريخ التزلج الحر: من المتمردين إلى الأبطال", "ja": "フリースタイルスキーの歴史：反逆者からチャンピオンへ", "zh": "Ziyou Shi Huaxue Lishi: Cong Panluanzhe dao Guanjun", "ko": "프리스타일 스키의 역사: 반항아에서 챔피언으로"}'::jsonb,
    '{"en": "Freestyle skiing emerged from skiers who broke the rules, performing acrobatic tricks that traditional skiing rejected. Today it''s one of the most exciting disciplines in winter sports.", "de": "Freestyle-Skiing entstand aus Skifahrern, die die Regeln brachen und akrobatische Tricks zeigten.", "fr": "Le ski freestyle est né de skieurs qui ont enfreint les règles, réalisant des figures acrobatiques.", "it": "Lo sci freestyle è nato da sciatori che infrangevano le regole, eseguendo acrobazie.", "es": "El esquí estilo libre surgió de esquiadores que rompieron las reglas, realizando trucos acrobáticos.", "pt": "O esqui estilo livre surgiu de esquiadores que quebraram as regras, realizando truques acrobáticos.", "nl": "Freestyle skiën ontstond uit skiërs die de regels braken en acrobatische trucs uitvoerden.", "ar": "ظهر التزلج الحر من المتزلجين الذين كسروا القواعد، وأدوا حركات بهلوانية", "ja": "フリースタイルスキーは、ルールを破りアクロバティックなトリックを披露するスキーヤーから生まれました。", "zh": "Ziyoushi huaxue yuanyu dapo guize de huaxue zhe, tamen biaoxian zaji dongzuo.", "ko": "프리스타일 스키는 규칙을 깨고 곡예 기술을 선보인 스키어들에게서 시작되었습니다."}'::jsonb,
    '{"en": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">Freestyle skiing</a> began as an act of rebellion. While traditional alpine skiing emphasized speed and precision, a group of daring skiers in the 1960s started adding flips, spins, and aerials to their runs. The skiing establishment dismissed them as \"hot doggers,\" but they would eventually transform winter sports.</p><h2>The Hot Dog Era</h2><p>In the 1960s and 1970s, young American skiers began experimenting with acrobatic moves. They performed on mogul fields, jumped off bumps, and added ballet-like moves to their skiing. The first freestyle competitions emerged in the United States, far from traditional European ski racing.</p><p>Early events combined ballet skiing, mogul skiing, and aerials into combined competitions. Films like \"Blizzard of Aahhh''s\" captured the counter-culture spirit of the movement.</p><h2>Road to Recognition</h2><p>For years, freestyle skiing operated outside official channels. The FIS initially rejected the discipline as too dangerous and too far from traditional skiing. Gradually, safety improvements and growing popularity changed attitudes.</p><p>Mogul skiing was recognized first, with the FIS World Cup starting in 1980. The discipline was included in the 1992 Winter Games, marking freestyle''s official arrival.</p><h2>Discipline Evolution</h2><p>Today''s freestyle skiing encompasses multiple disciplines:</p><p><strong>Moguls:</strong> Athletes ski through fields of bumps at speed while performing aerial tricks. Judged on turns, air, and speed.</p><p><strong>Aerials:</strong> Acrobatic jumping from specially built ramps, with athletes performing multiple flips and twists.</p><p><strong>Halfpipe:</strong> Adapted from snowboarding, athletes perform tricks while moving between the walls of a U-shaped course.</p><p><strong>Slopestyle:</strong> Athletes navigate a course of rails, jumps, and features, performing tricks throughout.</p><p><strong>Ski Cross:</strong> Multiple skiers race head-to-head down a course with jumps, rollers, and banked turns.</p><h2>Big Air Arrives</h2><p>Big air, featuring a single massive jump where athletes perform their most spectacular tricks, has become one of the sport''s signature events. Urban venues and spectacular settings have brought freestyle skiing to new audiences.</p><h2>Great Champions</h2><p>Johnny Moseley''s dinner roll at the 1998 Games electrified audiences. Shaun White crossed over from snowboarding to dominate halfpipe. The French team has produced exceptional aerialists, while mogul skiers from Canada, Japan, and Australia have achieved legendary status.</p><h2>Modern Era</h2><p>Freestyle skiing now attracts some of the world''s best athletes. Events like the X Games showcase the sport''s progression, with athletes constantly pushing the boundaries of what''s possible on skis.</p><p>The discipline that started as rebellion is now firmly established in winter sports'' mainstream, though it retains its creative, progressive spirit.</p>", "de": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">Freestyle-Skiing</a> begann als Rebellion. Während traditionelles alpines Skifahren Geschwindigkeit und Präzision betonte, begannen mutige Skifahrer in den 1960ern, Saltos und Drehungen hinzuzufügen.</p><h2>Die Hot-Dog-Ära</h2><p>In den 1960ern und 1970ern begannen junge amerikanische Skifahrer mit akrobatischen Bewegungen zu experimentieren.</p><h2>Disziplin-Entwicklung</h2><p>Heutiges Freestyle-Skiing umfasst mehrere Disziplinen: Buckelpiste, Aerials, Halfpipe, Slopestyle und Ski Cross.</p>", "fr": "<p>Le <a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">ski freestyle</a> a commencé comme un acte de rébellion. Alors que le ski alpin traditionnel mettait l''accent sur la vitesse et la précision, un groupe de skieurs audacieux dans les années 1960 a commencé à ajouter des flips et des rotations.</p><h2>L''ère Hot Dog</h2><p>Dans les années 1960 et 1970, de jeunes skieurs américains ont commencé à expérimenter des mouvements acrobatiques.</p><h2>Évolution des disciplines</h2><p>Le ski freestyle d''aujourd''hui comprend plusieurs disciplines : bosses, sauts acrobatiques, halfpipe, slopestyle et ski cross.</p>", "it": "<p>Lo <a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">sci freestyle</a> è iniziato come atto di ribellione. Mentre lo sci alpino tradizionale enfatizzava velocità e precisione, un gruppo di sciatori audaci negli anni ''60 iniziò ad aggiungere salti e rotazioni.</p><h2>L''era Hot Dog</h2><p>Negli anni ''60 e ''70, giovani sciatori americani iniziarono a sperimentare movimenti acrobatici.</p>", "es": "<p>El <a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">esquí estilo libre</a> comenzó como un acto de rebelión. Mientras el esquí alpino tradicional enfatizaba la velocidad y la precisión, un grupo de esquiadores atrevidos en los años 60 comenzó a agregar saltos y giros.</p>", "pt": "<p>O <a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">esqui estilo livre</a> começou como um ato de rebelião. Enquanto o esqui alpino tradicional enfatizava velocidade e precisão, um grupo de esquiadores ousados nos anos 1960 começou a adicionar saltos e giros.</p>", "nl": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">Freestyle skiën</a> begon als een daad van rebellie. Terwijl traditioneel alpineskiën snelheid en precisie benadrukte, begonnen gedurfde skiërs in de jaren 60 met het toevoegen van flips en spins.</p>", "ar": "<p>بدأ <a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">التزلج الحر</a> كعمل تمردي. بينما ركز التزلج الألبي التقليدي على السرعة والدقة، بدأ مجموعة من المتزلجين الجريئين في الستينيات بإضافة القلبات والدورات.</p>", "ja": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">フリースタイルスキー</a>は反逆の行為として始まりました。伝統的なアルペンスキーがスピードと精度を重視する中、1960年代の大胆なスキーヤーたちがフリップやスピンを加え始めました。</p>", "zh": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">Ziyoushi huaxue</a> zuowei panpan xingwei kaishi. Dangshi chuantong gaoshan huaxue qiangdiao sudu he jingque, er yiqun danxing de huaxue zhe zai 20 shiji 60 niandai kaishi tianjia fanteng he xuanzhuan.</p>", "ko": "<p><a href=\"/freestyle-skiing-guide/\">프리스타일 스키</a>는 반항의 행위로 시작되었습니다. 전통적인 알파인 스키가 속도와 정밀함을 강조하는 동안, 1960년대의 대담한 스키어들이 플립과 스핀을 추가하기 시작했습니다.</p>"}'::jsonb,
    'historical',
